// Title: Visual Studio Code Tunnel Shell Execution
// ID: f4a623c2-4ef5-4c33-b811-0642f702c9f1
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-10-25
// Tags: attack.command-and-control, attack.t1071.001
// Description: Detects the execution of a shell (powershell, bash, wsl...) via Visual Studio Code tunnel. Attackers can abuse this functionality to establish a C2 channel and execute arbitrary commands on the system.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((where(ParentImage ICONTAINS "\\servers\\Stable-") AND where(ParentImage IENDSWITH "\\server\\node.exe") AND where(ParentCommandLine ICONTAINS ".vscode-server")) AND (((where(Image IENDSWITH "\\powershell.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\pwsh.exe")) AND where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\terminal\\browser\\media\\shellIntegration.ps1")) OR ((where(Image IENDSWITH "\\wsl.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\bash.exe")))))
